 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "P1: the kernel is a lisse rank-one character sheaf",
 "statement": "The Fourier kernel $\\mathcal K_\\psi$ of [def-fd-kernel] is lisse of rank one on\n$V_0\\times_{S_0}V_0^\\vee$ and of finite Tor amplitude\n([def-weil-finite-tor-amplitude]), and\n\n$$\n\\mathcal K_\\psi\\otimes\\mathcal K_{\\psi'}\\cong\\mathcal K_{\\psi\\psi'},\n\\qquad\n\\mathcal K_\\psi^{-1}\\cong\\mathcal K_{\\psi^{-1}} .\n$$\n\n(Blueprint def:fd-kernel with lem:fd-as-lisse; the\npurity of the kernel is a weight-theoretic statement and is not used here.)",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-fourier-transform/sk-prop-kernel-lisse/prop-kernel-lisse.md",
  "place": "node prop-kernel-lisse, order 2695"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-fd-kernel",
  "def-weil-finite-tor-amplitude"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "$\\mathcal K_\\psi=b^*\\mathcal L_\\psi=\\mathcal L_{\\psi,b}$ is the inverse\nimage along the pairing $b:V_0\\times_{S_0}V_0^\\vee\\to\\mathbf A^1$ of the\nArtin–Schreier sheaf $\\mathcal L_\\psi$ on $\\mathbf A^1$, i.e. the Artin–Schreier\nsheaf of the function $b$ ([def-fd-kernel]); inverse images of\nlisse rank-one sheaves are lisse of rank one, so [lem-fd-as-lisse]\napplies verbatim, the value of the character being additive in the defining\nfunction. Lissity of rank one gives finite Tor amplitude, which is what the\ndefinition of the transform needs.",
   "uses": [
    "def-fd-kernel",
    "lem-fd-as-lisse"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
 "proof_deps": [
  "def-fd-kernel",
